// A QUALIFIED `extern` NAME — `extern def Q.member(…)` and `extern def Q[A].member(…)`. UniML has
// read this since before v3's own parser did, so `std/streams-bridge.ssc` parsed on the default
// front and died on v3's with `expected an expression, found .` — one language, two answers,
// decided by which front is registered (invariant I-3).
//
// The form is not exotic: `std/` declares six of them — `Bench.opaque`, `Source[A].distributed`,
// `DStream[A].local`, `DStream[A].localBounded`, `Source[A].remote`, `DStream[A].remote` — and
// ZERO qualified `def` names appear WITHOUT `extern` in `std/` or the conformance corpus, which is
// why the parser accepts the dot only on the extern path.
//
// Declared and NOT called on purpose: an extern no lane implements is refused at its CALL, so
// calling one here would test that refusal instead of this parse. The type params on the qualifier
// are consumed and discarded like every other type at Tier 0.
extern def Source.plain(x: Int): Int
extern def Source[A].distributed(partitions: Int): Int

def main() = println("qualified extern parsed")
